            "review_title": "Review at Japanese Udon Donnosuke Mi Vang",
            "review_text": "desiremmwekb10\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam2964 contributions\n0\nBig portion, good udon, so so other items\nNov 2018 • Family\nHumongous bowl with big portion created a good impression. I like the hot soup of Udon noodle. The beef was good, some of the toppings were not really good at all. Making the whole bowl of udon noodle a mixed satisfaction and disappointment combination. Me personally, I prefer ramen over udon. The big portion of udon noodle here was too much for me to handle. Well, I think the chef put a great deal of effort into making these udon noodle. For some people, they would enjoy it a lot more than I do. As for the sashimi and fried chicken, it was mediocre at best. Udon probably the signature dish, stick with it and order a small size (M) so that you could enjoy it fully.\nRead more\nWritten November 30, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
