            "review_text": "david o\n18 contributions\n0\nGood value, friendly staff\nAug 2018 • Couples\nImpressed, always a good sign when a restaurant’s customer base is reflective of the nationality of the food. At this restaurant you always see Japanese families and groups tucking into a bow of udon, and boy is there a lot to tuck into. The servings are HUGE and I mean big by big standards, we’re talking over sized bowls that can be used as serving dishes. The udon is of a high quality and there are an assortment of further dishes on the menu such as sushi, tempura, salads, beef bowls. Has the full range of Japanes dishes, but the irons are the main event, and did I mention you can automatically upsize your bowl of udon at mo extra charge...good value, definitely will fill you up. High quality foods. Long may it continue.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 5, 2018",
